1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,110
Listen to a talk in a sociology class.

2
00:00:05,110 --> 00:00:08,820
Social capital is the network of relationships among people

3
00:00:08,820 --> 00:00:11,090
who live and work in a particular society.

4
00:00:11,090 --> 00:00:14,220
These networks enable society to function effectively.

5
00:00:14,220 --> 00:00:19,888
Social capital includes things like trust, mutual understanding and shared values,

6
00:00:19,888 --> 00:00:25,040
and also behaviors that bind people together and facilitate cooperation.

7
00:00:25,040 --> 00:00:28,500
Social capital can be divided into two main types

8
00:00:28,500 --> 00:00:32,150
bonding social capital and bridging social capital.

9
00:00:32,150 --> 00:00:36,830
Bonding social capital refers to the tight bonds within a close-knit group,

10
00:00:36,830 --> 00:00:39,170
like family members or close friends.

11
00:00:39,170 --> 00:00:42,500
These strong ties are essential for providing support

12
00:00:42,500 --> 00:00:44,200
and assistance during times of need.

13
00:00:44,200 --> 00:00:47,533
Bridging social capital, on the other hand,

14
00:00:47,533 --> 00:00:50,600
involves connections that transcend different social groups

15
00:00:51,100 --> 00:00:55,150
like relationships between acquaintances or colleagues from different backgrounds.

16
00:00:55,150 --> 00:01:00,250
These weaker ties are crucial for accessing new information and opportunities.

17
00:01:00,250 --> 00:01:05,000
The benefits of social capital are numerous.

18
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:07,545
It can give people emotional support,

19
00:01:07,545 --> 00:01:12,210
increase their access to resources and information and foster communal cooperation.

20
00:01:12,210 --> 00:01:14,275
And interestingly, people and communities

21
00:01:14,275 --> 00:01:19,230
with higher levels of social capital actually tend to have better health.

22
00:01:19,230 --> 00:01:23,320
Next, we will discuss how social capital can be measured

23
00:01:23,320 --> 00:01:27,290
and the challenges associated with its quantification.
